            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the recent hospital admission of your patient, a 46-year-old male, admitted on 18/08/2020 with confirmed SARS-CoV-2 infection. On admission, he presented with fever, dry cough, and progressive dyspnoea. Chest X-ray and CT confirmed bilateral pneumonia. Blood tests, arterial blood gases, and pulse oximetry revealed moderate hypoxaemia. He was treated with supplemental oxygen therapy, dexamethasone, and anticoagulation. Intravenous fluids were administered for supportive care. Clinical course was favourable with gradual improvement of respiratory function. Physiotherapy was initiated prior to discharge. The patient was educated regarding post-COVID recovery and infection precautions. He is discharged in a recovering state and will require outpatient follow-up including respiratory function monitoring. Please do not hesitate to contact me should you require further information.</div>"
            },
